---
import { stackChips } from "../data/site";
---

<section id="about">
  <div class="wrap about-inner">
    <div class="col">
      <p class="eyebrow">README.md</p>
      <h2 class="section-title">About</h2>
            <p class="bio">
        Hey, I'm Mohamed. I've always been drawn to computers and to making
        things with them — so I started learning HTML and CSS back in 2018,
        and never really stopped. Since then I've picked up JavaScript,
        Python, Flask, and Figma along the way, and by now the two sides
        have merged: I don't build a site and hand it off for a "designer"
        to skin, and I don't design a brand without knowing what it takes
        to ship it.
      </p>
      <p class="bio">
        In 2026 that means full-stack web development and graphic design
        under one process — interfaces, brand identity, and the motion and
        content that carries them, built and designed by the same person
        end to end.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="col">
      <p class="eyebrow">stack.json</p>
      <ul class="chips mono">
        {stackChips.map((chip) => (
          <li>{chip}</li>
        ))}
      </ul>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<style>
  .about-inner {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1.3fr 1fr;
    gap: 60px;
  }

  .bio {
    font-size: 15.5px;
    line-height: 1.75;
    color: var(--text-dim);
    max-width: 52ch;
  }

  .chips {
    list-style: none;
    margin: 8px 0 0;
    padding: 0;
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 8px;
  }

  .chips li {
    font-size: 12.5px;
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: var(--radius);
    padding: 8px 12px;
    color: var(--text-dim);
  }

  @media (max-width: 720px) {
    .about-inner {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
      gap: 36px;
    }
  }
</style>
